  "body_html": "<h1>Von Neumann Minimax Theorem</h1>\n<p>Every finite two-player zero-sum matrix game has a value in mixed strategies:</p>\n<p>$$\\max_x \\min_j E_A(x,j) = \\min_y \\max_i E_A(i,y).$$</p>\n<p>Equivalently, there are optimal mixed strategies $x^\\ast$ and $y^\\ast$ and a\nvalue $v$ such that player I guarantees at least $v$ against every column and\nplayer II holds player I to at most $v$ against every row.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Chapter 2, Theorem 2.3.1] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MechDesign.pdf</code>. Von Neumann minimax theorem for finite zero-sum games.</li>\n</ul>",
